r/production, ER task check, AEP task check and applicable site/workflow validation). Root may sequence qualified dependency pins between gates; no dependency is called fully accepted from a partial check. Original full review budgets and external provider qualification stay unchanged; no new micro-review around denied administration work.\n\nSOURCE-ONLY initially. No Cargo/build/fixture until root allocation. First deliver source-ready diff and exact necessary lock/pin sequencing; root freezes only after applicable gates and supplies exact commit objects for downstream pins. Do not invent commits, publish, or hand-edit lock dependency IDs. Evidence/scratch belongs under this directory, list all paths. No old fixture environment reuse.\n\nStop this companion after one coherent exact dependency vector with all required acceptance, source/check manifests and teardown report, release companion leases and return exclusively to the unchanged complete M7 contract. No additional compatibility wishlist or unrelated consumer promotion. Existing complete M7 acceptance remains mandatory; this companion alone closes no top-level milestone.\n\n## Source-verified semantic correction\n\nThe original row-shaped ER wrapper was an architectural defect: it persisted generic replace operations instead of authored domain commands. Source correction now maps existing authored entities/commands, with only the three already-justified typed homes and DispatchAdmission reuse. Root's inspection additionally found arbitrary lifecycle reconstruction and blanket decision/reason inputs; those paths were corrected within this same M7 assignment. Missing terminal entities refuse, and the sole two-stage DispatchAdmission creation requires explicit successful capture_read/capture_revalidation provenance. Reasons come from retained facts. No fabricated legacy history is admitted.\n\nAuthor source-only checkpoint is .local/evidence/m7-source-handoff.md in managed ess-evolution-connectors-adoption-20260