shes, the four changed files and39 unchanged original handoff files (prior manifest f932e8819a567b8db2d31eaddec07ba8bbc5ac4f527c4b994f2f96446996fb92). Selected-file rustfmt1.91.1 and diff checks exited0. This is source evidence only; no fixture or runtime case executed. Generated entity-runtime-definitions.json remains ABSENT, so the source remains uncompiled and M7 unaccepted.\n\nThe bounded fixture edit is finished. Remaining M7 acceptance is unchanged: coherent qualified Eventlog→ER→AEP SQLite pins/locks incorporating original M2/M3 corrections; exact authored definition generation and drift; existing migration levels1–8, actual ER transitions/replay/rebuild, owner/CLI/provider/Secret Service acceptance; full gate/minima/site/common, original review and integration. No new worker assignment/review round or accounting requirement. Source-only/build/cleanup stop remains while storage custody is UNASSIGNED.\n\nM2/M3 corrections are composed into the existing ER/AEP SQLite companions; all25 desired hashes match. Eventlog Cargo-generated lock resolution and locked/offline Linux-host metadata both exit0, selecting rusqlite0.40.2/libsqlite3-sys0.38.2. Vendored header declares SQLite3.53.2; existing Connectors >=3.51.3 guard is unchanged. WebAssembly packages appear in the cross-target lock but not the host metadata graph. This establishes source dependency selection only: rusqlite declares no fixed MSRV, so actual supported-minimum checks remain required. ER/AEP locks still await actual qualified upstream commits; generated M7 definitions remain absent. No build/fixture allocation or acceptance claim. Receipt: home-path:sha256:503775221545c8b7c162ecd125564db1748c82f0c41c895d322bbf716d5d3ec1 Storage custody UNASSIGNED; existing build and cleanup stops remain. Original completion contract and review limits unchanged.\n\n## Coherent SQLite candidate acceptance\n\nRoot begins original coherent SQLite compatibility acceptance after composing accepted M2 final open/provision and M3 capture/selector corrections. Exact current Eventlog companion has8changed source/manifest/test paths; source-preflight.json binds them. Default bash scripts/gate.sh is running on Rust1.91 with exported actual disposable PostgreSQL, locked/offline, one Cargo job/one test thread. Production-proof mode and declared checks remain required before freezing its local source candidate; then exact ER/AEP downstream pins/locks and their original gates, followed by M7 generation/runtime acceptance. No hidden path override, no SQLite guard downgrade, and no manual lockfile edits.\n\nThis is the already-approved dependency compatibility contract, not a new review or prerequisite. Existing administration review restriction and original remaining provider native gaps still block qualified integration; compatibility gates cannot clear them. Root owns a temporary measured-capacity provider lane, separate cache and disposable fixture; cleanup/custody follows each closed component. Current S8 native and M3 file-reader assignments stay finite and separate. No publication or real-store cutover.\n\n## Coherent SQLite dependency acceptance — 2026-09-17T06:30Z\n\nEventlog6d5e249b83552b3417ce5b0c883999c95d304db4 passed both required actual-PostgreSQL gates, with accepted existing-open correction composed, and signed common check/verify. ER6a960962dd660d1e828797b7eb9c1db879ccad96 passed full actual-PG task check (including runtime1.91), pure1.85 build and site-build, then common check/verify. Both candidates are local/unpublished; source hashes remain exact. Qualified M1/M2 integration remains subject to the recorded provider administration restriction and original qualification stages. Exact freezes: home-path:sha256:caa2ae49e0156344a66cb923f72bc6dc1628c0da0435994111348d2288323305,er-acceptance}/freeze.json.\n\nRoot composed those exact Git pins into AEP and Connectors and used package-scoped Cargo-generated locks, preserving unrelated registry pins. Connectors root lock now resolves the preserved SQLite0.40.2/native0.38.2 dependency; no generation/runtime success is inferred. AEP full task check is running against owned PostgreSQL with final capture and legacy-reader source corrections. AEP tool pin follows only after freeze. Existing complete M7 contract still requires authored generation, actual lifecycle/migration/owner/CLI/Secret Service acceptance, excluded workspace and full gate, original reviews and qualified integration. No new author assignment or review scope.\n\nCheckpoint cleanup retired exact ER compiler/site outputs2,818,977,792bytes with13source hashes and clean status reverified; Eventlog and reader cache receipts are separate. Root retains PG for the sequential AEP component; S8 uses the other bounded lane. Generated definitions must come from the existing Rust generator, never hand-written output.\n\n## Resume the original whole M7 completion — 2026-09-17\n\nThe original43-path partial source handoff is resumed by home-path:sha256:7d783c55a0ebdc7123ae50bc0c8dc44ba1aa06418e394e29ae9cc43f5acef4ff under home-path:sha256:f85465a5fb40e0f3bf9a9b5ec00e0dddf0ff38a730dbc7359383886e6c987e0f and the unchanged complete-adoption-contract.md. Its former M2 assignment remains closed. Existing approved scope/typed source ownership unchanged; no new prerequisite or review. Root owns AEP tool pin until final upstream freeze, planning and integration. Worker starts source-only; after root explicitly releases the AEP build lane it owns one max2job/1thread Connectors acceptance lane beside S8, with existing floors and exact owned disposable fixtures. Stop at all required original M7 author acceptance plus source/generated/check/evidence and teardown handoff; no further scope after closure. Final independent reviews/qualified integration remain root-owned.\n\n# Existing union preservation correction\n\nOwner: Astra, under existing Connectors `story:ess-evolution-er-metadata-adoption` and approved ESS-EVOLUTION.md §§6–7. Author: sdk_final_obligation_correction; its previous reader assignment remains closed. This corrects an observed M7 blocker, not a new product capability or review project.\n\nEvidence: `metadata-entities-retry6.log` in `/var/tmp/ess-evolution-m7-acceptance-20260917/logs` refuses existing OperationDeclaration Parameter/BodyParameter unions. Exact ESS b5e validation succeeds. ServiceConfiguration.adapter and the closure through AdapterSpecification, OperationDeclaration and Source predate this initiative; preserve them, all 21 required definitions and existing wire bytes. ER6a960962 validation.rs:2255–2268 incorrectly treats a nested object's `value` member as colliding with its containing union's adjacent payload key. ESS ess-gen types.rs:696–733 and ER validate_union:2658 onward use separate object levels. ER design §10.1 and R145 contain a contradictory collision sentence that must be corrected explicitly against the original exact ESS semantic-reuse requirement. Do not introduce reference-only projections, rename fields, drop relations, or relax malformed-value validation.\n\nDeliverable: smallest source/design/register/changelog correction preserving unambiguous adjacent unions, including tags `kind` and `value` and payload members named `value`/`content`. Show old-source failure on the actual nested shape, corrected registration/create/operation/record replay with exact retained nested bytes, and named malformed-tag/type/extra-member refusals. Retain existing kernel/1 refusal and service semantics. No new dependencies or format change without demonstrating a meaning/byte consequence.\n\nManaged tree: `home-path:sha256:97be6bf3b07dbad69197f81f9d53f0ee0e3614a658be2f70153581da1cd7112b`, base6a960962dd660d1e828797b7eb9c1db879ccad96. Source scope: entity-core validation and behavior tests, existing service semantics design, requirements register, CHANGELOG only. Root owns planning, local freeze, downstream pins and final integration. No denied administration-review work, reviewer assignmen