e.\n\nM7 author holds compilation while this worker owns its previous build slot; S9 owns the other slot. Max2jobs1testthread, outside-Git TMP,20GiB disk/16GiBRAM floors. Bounded separate target; no sharing live S9 target, no children. Preserve small logs; idle reproducible cleanup after completion. No new independent review round.\n\n# Coherent ESS target-pin composition\n\nLocal candidate d65ef449a2c4fb08721df56587ba86c886337db0 is exactly three substitutions from ESS9aa8: workspace entity-core revision, its sole Cargo.lock source identity, and ENTITY_RUNTIME_REVISION all name ER13b8a1faddcbd368ca636606efa9e4927a9221c8. No lowering behavior or unrelated lock change. Fuzz lock has no entity-core entry. ER entity-core tree object c0f42da0b536d2fb03e73b448181b719f6595b25 is identical at28d and13b.\n\nLocked offline metadata, affected lowerer tests, strict affected Clippy, targeted lowerer formatting and repository task fmt-check passed. The initially used cargo fmt --all reports existing byte-pinned generated Rust, which the repository's own task deliberately excludes; no generated bytes were rewritten. Exact source/log manifests are candidate-source.sha256/evidence.sha256. Full final consumer-enabled ESS/site qualification remains pending, not waived by local candidate acceptance.\n\nRoot applied only those same three substitutions to canonical ESS, preserving its other work; preimages/hashes retained under canonical-before/. Locked offline canonical metadata exited0 with exactly one HTTPS entity-core13b8, and git diff --check exited0. S9 native author applied the same substitutions before final native freeze. No full manifest/lock overwrite or new review pass.\n\nSigned common evidence is now verified for this exact ESS candidate: common-receipt.json, common-check-2.log and common-verify.log. The worker's standalone attempt initially failed because the default policy file was absent; root source-checked the CLI and used the existing installed hook configuration's p