adata adoption while preserving existing behavior. This is one dependency-coherence companion inside the still-open complete M7 author assignment. It is not an extension of the CLOSED M2/M3 authors and not a provider-administration examination.\n\n## Concrete failure and insufficient old evidence\n\nConnectors baseline4e7f5b8 crates/connectors-host/Cargo.toml pins rusqlite=0.40.2; production local/metadata.rs refuses version_number below3_051_003. Eventlog088c27b5 Cargo.toml and ER5df62103 crates/entity-sqlite/Cargo.toml select rusqlite0.37. AEPa80a95f4 Cargo.toml also selects0.37. Locally installed libsqlite3-sys0.35.0 bundled header declares3.50.2/3050002; libsqlite3-sys0.38.2 declares3.53.2/3053002. The native SQLite links identity makes these lines incompatible in a single consumer. Downgrading Connectors would make its preserved admission guard refuse. Prior independent component gates never composed this complete consumer dependency closure and cannot prove it works.\n\nRoot confirmed exact manifests and guard/header values. No new external advisory is asserted here: preserving the existing explicit admission requirement is sufficient. This blocks M7 compile/acceptance and final coherent vector, not source-only metadata implementation, the original ER/AEP source reviews or current SDK correction.\n\n## Exact source ownership\n\nWorker connectors_metadata_adoption, no children; root sole AEP writer/freezer/integrator. Acquire distinct leases; read each AGENTS before edits. Use only these fresh managed companion trees, never frozen original submissions:\n\n- Eventlog managed-worktrees/eventlog/ess-evolution-sqlite-compatibility-20260916, base088c27b5df9745c68d8a2240dbb2038998b03efe: Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, existing SQLite tests and only concrete API compatibility edits if compiler requires them, associated changelog.\n- ER managed-worktrees/entity-runtime/ess-evolution-er-sqlite-compatibility-20260916, base5df62103b129ef482f9fdafc3cb3f7c194c7b942: entity-sqlite/C