ead each AGENTS before edits. Use only these fresh managed companion trees, never frozen original submissions:\n\n- Eventlog managed-worktrees/eventlog/ess-evolution-sqlite-compatibility-20260916, base088c27b5df9745c68d8a2240dbb2038998b03efe: Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, existing SQLite tests and only concrete API compatibility edits if compiler requires them, associated changelog.\n- ER managed-worktrees/entity-runtime/ess-evolution-er-sqlite-compatibility-20260916, base5df62103b129ef482f9fdafc3cb3f7c194c7b942: entity-sqlite/Cargo.toml, workspace/Eventlog revision declarations, Cargo.lock, existing SQLite tests and only compiler-required API compatibility, associated changelog.\n- AEP managed-worktrees/aep/ess-evolution-aep-sqlite-compatibility-20260916, basea80a95f4b3ae7712708438ccbd8dc3f95dbe1bbb: Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock and exact ER/Eventlog revision declarations, existing SQLite backend tests and only compiler-required compatibility, associated changelog.\n\nOwn metadata/Connectors source remains in the original M7 tree. Preserve all journals; no planning files in companion edits. Root records external scope on the existing Connectors owner, with workspace-relative sibling source paths. No other worker may mutate these companion trees.\n\n## Deliverable and checks\n\nSelect the existing Connectors exact rusqlite0.40.2/native0.38.2 line consistently, preserving bundled selection and the >=3.51.3 guard. No storage/schema/envelope reinterpretation, force-resolved native duplicate, hidden path override, vendored registry mutation, removal of guard, generic upgrade or minimum bump. Preserve pure ER/AEP1.85 boundaries; runtime1.91. Let Cargo generate locks. If actual compiler/API constraints contradict these boundaries, report the exact conflict and bounded alternative before choosing semantics.\n\nImplement only necessary dependency/API compatibility. Verify actual SQLite version and real File/SQLite reopen, retries/transactions/import/projection behavior through existing a