andidate is not landing or qualified integration and does not waive them. State the exact qualification boundary in the handoff.\n\nManaged tree home-path:sha256:d14c66c81e712ca570f50ed7af06139a3dd47e1bc1ca0cc1611473883e3a19c0, exactbase9aa8. Acquire own lease/read AGENTS. Root owns AEP and final canonical adoption. Use standalone bot only for an exact local source freeze if its common gate permits; no publish, hook bypass, policy change or denied-work retry. Do not touch the pending five generated-digest exception policy. Stop after one minimal checked source/lock/target vector and local candidate handoff, or a concrete exact refusal. Root/M7 then composes ordinary HTTPS ER13b8+newESS, regenerates the real bundle and proves both lock graphs plus original public journeys. No source-only milestone replaces M7 acceptance.\n\nM7 author holds compilation while this worker owns its previous build slot; S9 owns the other slot. Max2jobs1testthread, outside-Git TMP,20GiB disk/16GiBRAM floors. Bounded separate target; no sharing live S9 target, no children. Preserve small logs; idle reproducible cleanup after completion. No new independent review round.\n\n# Coherent ESS target-pin composition\n\nLocal candidate d65ef449a2c4fb08721df56587ba86c886337db0 is exactly three substitutions from ESS9aa8: workspace entity-core revision, its sole Cargo.lock source identity, and ENTITY_RUNTIME_REVISION all name ER13b8a1faddcbd368ca636606efa9e4927a9221c8. No lowering behavior or unrelated lock change. Fuzz lock has no entity-core entry. ER entity-core tree object c0f42da0b536d2fb03e73b448181b719f6595b25 is identical at28d and13b.\n\nLocked offline metadata, affected lowerer tests, strict affected Clippy, targeted lowerer formatting and repository task fmt-check passed. The initially used cargo fmt --all reports existing byte-pinned generated Rust, which the repository's own task deliberately excludes; no generated bytes were rewritten. Exact source/log manifests are candidate-source.sha