ities/cardinality or hide it in arbitrary JSON. A genuine missing semantic must identify which numbered requirement above it blocks, the exact counterexample, bounded deliverable and stopping condition.\n\nCurrent source owners include crates/connectors-host/src/local/metadata.rs and metadata/*.sql; registry and its lifecycle/observation/revalidation/use-and-retirement modules; runtime/state; mutations; audit; approvals; approval_keys; approval_policy; owner and keyring integration. Generation owners are crates/connectors-spec/toolchain.json, crates/connectors-build/aep-toolchain.json and cli/gate/tool-resolution code, apps/connectors/spec and the excluded apps/connectors-cli-contract generated workspace. Read exact callers before edits; update authored bindings and generators rather than hand-editing generated Rust.\n\n## Acceptance and exact stopping condition\n\nThe author closes this assignment after all of the following pass on one final source vector and one report connects each result to the actual entrypoint:\n\n- Nonempty legacy metadata migration and fresh setup both reach the ER/Eventlog authority; exact preserved identity/reference/revision/fence/audit comparisons, interrupted migration resume, subsequent real mutations, close/reopen and derived projection rebuild pass. Prove no remaining independently authoritative direct-SQL writer in the selected production paths.\n- Actual separate-process CLI/owner acceptance covers the existing catalog/GitLab, Kubernetes and PostgreSQL local journeys under disposable providers: protected connect/repair, saved connection reuse after CLI/owner/keyring restart, passive status/list, bounded queries, competing repair/revoke and dispatch races, stop suppression, known refusal and uncertain outcome without duplicate external dispatch. Use existing registered cases when they cover the change; add only cases for actual migration/semantic gaps.\n- Explicitly run the qualified disposable Secret Service cases, including `disposable_secret_service_restart_and_failures` and `disposable_registry_publication_cli_and_retirement_restart`, with an owned bus/keyring/TMPDIR and the actual candidate CONNECTORS_TEST_CLI. Ordinary tests ignore these and cannot substitute for them. Preserve the admitted GNOME Keyring binding and credential redaction controls. Teardown only exact owned children/state after terminal checks.\n- Validate/generate every affected shared/native ESS root and CLI binding under the exact pin; generated drift and both lockfile/workspace builds pass. Demonstrate the retained AEP correction or its verified upstream equivalent.\n- Run the exact full `cargo run --locked -p connectors-build -- gate --msrv`, including applicable runtime1.91 and retained pure minima. No waiver for strict checks, boundaries, pin mismatch, missing roots or excluded workspace. Run affected documentation/website validation if its authored surface changes, as repository instructions require.\n- Produce one final report with requirement-to-entrypoint-to-evidence mapping, exact baseline/final source and dependency pins, source/generated/check manifests, commands/exits, remaining external limitations, and owned-resource teardown. Preserve all unrelated source/planning and baseline integrity. Root then freezes and independently examines the whole delivery under the existing orchestration rules; author completion does not imply provider qualification or integration.\n\nDo not keep extending the author assignment once these deliverables/checks are satisfied. Report a specific source failure for correction within this same outcome; unrelated improvements require a separately justified assignment. No test-count-only acceptance, provisional implementation labeled integrated, release, deployment or real provider effect is authorized by this contract.\n\n## Dependencies and scheduling\n\nImplementation and disposable migration/CLI acceptance can proceed against exact candidate ER/ESS/AEP interfaces once root selects them. Final M7 verification/integration depends on qualified M1/M2 providers and final applicable source pins; consumer cases do not clear the separate interrupted administration review. Actual planning-store cutover is M4e under the existing AEP migration owner, not silently performed by this author. M8 infrastructure comparison remains a separate approved acceptance outcome using independently observed facts; desired declarations are not observations.\n\nUse the prepared managed tree; acquire a distinct worker lease before edits. Root alone mutates its AEP store. Source work can start independently; heavy builds require the shared allocation, task-owned `.local/tmp`, bounded jobs and20GiBdisk/16GiBRAM floors. Maximum three workers across the initiative, no children.\n\n## Implementation dispatch\n\nImplementation is authorized under the existing approved ESS evolution scope and the complete M7 contract. Root is selecting the next available worker slot after the original SDK reviewer closes; no fourth worker is started.\n\nInitial exact candidate vector: Entity Runtime7fd93ef43d4a91c460c7305f9e3be90d7b0a4c11 with its coherent Eventlog43ceaa09ceec610e25891815e33e03e8df92ee28; ESSb5e980fe0aff382bca91a08ebd3827ee8ff4b73e; AEPa80a95f4b3ae7712708438ccbd8dc3f95dbe1bbb. Final applicable qualified revisions and whole gates remain required. Preserve the current AEP patch until actual equivalence is established; never mix crossing Rust types from distinct revisions.\n\nBegin the entire metadata migration and actual-entrypoint implementation source-only. Design the concrete compatible transition before its readers; preserve all existing identities, revisions, fences, custody references and audit facts. Root owns planning/integration and later resource allocation. No new provider, release, deployment or real planning-store cutover is part of this author contract. Administration/provider qualification remains external, and source preparation does not claim it resolved.\n\n## Required SQLite dependency compatibility\n\n# M7 SQLite dependency compatibility — bounded companion\n\nExisting owner story:ess-evolution-er-metadata-adoption; approved §7/M7 requires actual ER/Eventlog SQLite metadata adoption while preserving existing behavior. This is one dependency-coherence companion inside the still-open complete M7 author assignment. It is not an extension of the CLOSED M2/M3 authors and not a provider-administration examination.\n\n## Concrete failure and insufficient old evidence\n\nConnectors baseline4e7f5b8 crates/connectors-host/Cargo.toml pins rusqlite=0.40.2; production local/metadata.rs refuses version_number below3_051_003. Eventlog088c27b5 Cargo.toml and ER5df62103 crates/entity-sqlite/Cargo.toml select rusqlite0.37. AEPa80a95f4 Cargo.toml also selects0.37. Locally installed libsqlite3-sys0.35.0 bundled header declares3.50.2/3050002; libsqlite3-sys0.38.2 declares3.53.2/3053002. The native SQLite links identity makes these lines incompatible in a single consumer. Downgrading Connectors would make its preserved admission guard refuse. Prior independent component gates never composed this complete consumer dependency closure and cannot prove it works.\n\nRoot confirmed exact manifests and guard/header values. No new external advisory is asserted here: preserving the existing explicit admission requirement is sufficient. This blocks M7 compile/acceptance and final coherent vector, not source-only metadata implementation, the original ER/AEP source reviews or current SDK correction.\n\n## Exact source ownership\n\nWorker connectors_metadata_adoption, no children; root sole AEP writer/freezer/integrator. Acquire distinct leases; read each AGENTS before edits. Use only these fresh managed companion trees, never frozen original submissions:\n\n- Eventlog managed-worktrees/eventlog/ess-evolution-sqlite-compatibility-20260916, base088c27b5df9745c68d8a2240dbb2038998b03efe: Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, existing SQLite tests and only concrete API compa