ney acceptance is claimed. Original typed errors/exact validity evidence are being captured within the same M7 contract, without weakening assertions.\n\nPin worker assignment CLOSED, own lease released; managed source remains clean/local. Its idle1GiB home-path:sha256:08ce937436dc5fb50a4384c2b934cb39657e34821220dcfa193fa73445ae37ae is retained: automatic approval review rejected rm-style removal; cargo clean also refused its missing/invalid CACHEDIR.TAG. No equivalent cleanup retry authorized. This target is distinct from the successfully retired4.71GiB ER correction cache. Root retains custody; no managed-tree retirement/publication.\n","document":{"events":[{"args":{"command":"move-status","decided_on":"{\"recorded\":{\"test_result\":5}}","target":"ent-7b1c1cbdbd6fe0bc966e370b7f4944bf","to":"implemented"},"changed":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-7b1c1cbdbd6fe0bc966e370b7f4944bf","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/ess-evolution-er-metadata-adoption","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"human:timo"},"revision":31,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":1790338947906}},"status":"implemented"},"entity":"aep.entity","from_state":"active","id":"ent-7b1c1cbdbd6fe0bc966e370b7f4944bf","payload":{"actor":"human:timo","at":1790338947906,"causation":"cmd-child-c49ccedcb809c5f1113a6f4f575079436569ae5af599e2cdc46af596d249c2c9","correlation":"protocol-artifact-move","event_id":"aep.entity:ent-7b1c1cbdbd6fe0bc966e370b7f4944bf@31#0~37ae279b5e418f0e","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-25T12:22:27Z"},"revision":31,"to_state":"implemented","type":"aep.status.move/v1","version":1}],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-7b1c1cbdbd6fe0bc966e370b7f4944bf","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/ess-evolution-er-metadata-adoption","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"human:timo"},"revision":31,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":1790338947906}},"body":"# M7 — complete Connectors ER metadata adoption\n\nPrepared 2026-09-16 by root under approved ESS-EVOLUTION.md §7 and its verification/completion criteria. This is one whole delivery assignment, not a new prerequisite. No worker dispatched yet; maximum three existing workers remain occupied. Root owns planning, final source freeze and integration. Implementation remains local; publication, deployment, new providers and unrelated Connectors backlog are excluded.\n\n## Outcome and existing evidence\n\nThe production Connectors v2 local CLI and its host use ER over Eventlog SQLite for their local metadata authority, preserving existing identities, credential references, fences, revisions and audit history. The qualified Secret Service remains credential custody. Exact ESS/AEP tool selections, generated sources and both Cargo lockfile surfaces agree with the accepted source vector. Actual restart/repair/revoke/protected-input/query/uncertainty/redaction acceptance and the complete repository gate establish the outcome.\n\nBaseline: clean primary 4e7f5b8f8474d26274154f035a94836621351e60, rechecked before creating managed tree `ess-evolution-connectors-adoption-20260916`. Existing `story:ess3-format-adoption` covers a format/pin change only and does not own metadata adoption. Current metadata.rs and seven included SQL migrations still make direct SQLite the authority; changing database setup alone would leave the other writers unchanged. Historical provider and keyring acceptance does not prove the migrated authority. Read-only discovery is retained at verification/connectors-readiness-20260916.md.\n\nRead README.md, VISION.md, AGENTS.md and all of docs/design.md before implementation, then the current contracts and sources governing the affected ports. Root has done that discovery. Historical design stages and the broader complete-local-connectors initiative do not add new providers, MCP/Helm decisions, media, hosted federation or live sandbox work to this assignment.\n\n## Complete implementation contract\n\n1. **One metadata authority through the actual entrypoints.** Replace the currently authoritative writes/reads in local metadata, registry, runtime stop state, mutation attempts/keys, audit, approval spending, approval issuer/key metadata and local approval policy with ER over Eventlog SQLite. Route the real CLI/owner/host callers through that authority. SQLite projection storage may remain under its declared owner; it must not become a second independent mutable authority. Do not substitute a generic snapshot bag or wrapper that leaves direct SQL writes authoritative. Use the shared ER executor/kernel and supported atomic append groups; do not create another executor or product-specific persistence backend.\n2. **Preserve known semantics.** Keep binding publication/terminal revoke/final dispatch comparisons atomic under the same logical metadata authority. Keep mutation key reservation plus Prepared attempt, terminal settlement/replay state and retirement coupled as the selected contracts require. Approval spend, provider dispatch and custody remain separately acknowledged boundaries; no fabricated distributed transaction. Preserve exact approval/key/attempt identities, tombstones, stop suppression, private incarnation continuity, semantic revision, credential generation and private publication fence as distinct coordinates. Unacknowledged commits/read failures never authorize dispatch, publication, reuse or absence. Recovery observes the owning durable record and never resends an external effect solely because the owner restarted.\n3. **Explicit compatible local migration.** Define and implement a versioned transition from the currently recognized metadata schemas (levels1–8, installed by their admitted owners). Preserve authority/UID, existing state, audit order and retained safety facts without inventing historical events or global ordering absent from the source. Capture the legacy source under exclusive writer control, retain the recovery source, verify staged equivalence and switch to one selected authority. Reopening, interruption and retry must be deterministic and safe. Unknown/future/tampered schemas or mixed writer generations refuse without resetting state. Passive inspection still creates/migrates nothing. No automatic migration of the separately installed predecessor's configuration or credentials. Test disposable prior-version fixtures and the actual admitted CLI/host path; do not access a user's desktop keyring or real metadata for acceptance.\n4. **Keep custody and process behavior.** Secret Service owns credential material; metadata carries admitted opaque references only. Preserve protected terminal/file/stdin entry, one-use consumption, safe refusals and restored terminal echo. Preserve exact child ownership, supervision, startup coalescing, bounded shutdown, stop suppression and reuse across CLI/owner/keyring restarts. No secrets/private locators in generated public data, ordinary results, diagnostics, logs or retained public fixtures.\n5. **Exact generation and compiler compatibility.** Advance the single ESS pin and AEP tool pin to exact coordinator-selected candidates, then qualify the final accepted revisions before integration. Retain the current AEP patch (73d78e50369adf0853e457a226002bcc84e2b43a50903f28ed3e6afdd046e68f) until its behavior is proved equivalent upstream. Re-derive every actual ESS root rather than copying the stale count from the format story; version/content changes must follow the selected tool's real semantics. Regenerate from owning authored inputs. Verify root Cargo.lock and the excluded apps/connectors-cli-contract workspace/lockfile independently; root workspace success cannot cover an excluded workspace. Eventlog-backed runtime roots move to1.91; independent libraries retain their declared minima (currently1.88 for this repository) and corresponding checks. No blanket minimum increase or gate skip.\n\n## Existing typed homes and source ownership\n\nThis assignment migrates already modeled behavior; it introduces no speculative product entity. Existing typed homes include ess/domains/auth_bindings.yaml (Connection, Acquisition, CustodyVersion and references), mutations.yaml (attempt lifecycle), execution_audit.yaml, approval_issuers.yaml and local_approval_policy.yaml, plus the remaining registered shared domains. Existing CLI values live in ess/domains/cli.yaml. If an implementation requires a new persisted type or relation, model and validate that concrete requirement before code; do not guess identities/cardinality or hide it in arbitrary JSON. A genuine missing semantic must identify which numbered requirement above it blocks, the exact counterexample, bounded deliverable and stopping condition.\n\nCurrent source owners include crates/connectors-host/src/local/metadata.rs and metadata/*.sql; registry and its lifecycle/observation/revalidation/use-and-retirement modules; runtime/state; mutations; audit; approvals; approval_keys; approval_policy; owner and keyring integration. Generation owners are crates/connectors-spec/toolchain.json, crates/connectors-build/aep-toolchain.json and cli/gate/tool-resolution code, apps/connectors/spec and the excluded apps/connectors-cli-contract generated workspace. Read exact callers before edits; update authored bindings and generators rather than hand-editing generated Rust.\n\n## Acceptance and exact stopping condition\n\nThe author closes this assignment after all of the following pass on one final source vector and one report connects each result to the actual entrypoint:\n\n- Nonempty legacy metadata migration and fresh setup both reach the ER/Eventlog authority; exact preserved identity/reference/revision/fence/audit comparisons, interrupted migration resume, subsequent real mutations, close/reopen and derived projection rebuild pass. Prove no remaining independently authoritative direct-SQL writer in the selected production paths.\n- Actual separate-process CLI/owner acceptance covers the existing catalog/GitLab, Kubernetes and PostgreSQL local journeys under disposable providers: protected connect/repair, saved connection reuse after CLI/owner/keyring restart, passive status/list, bounded queries, competing repair/revoke and dispatch races, stop suppression, known refusal and uncertain outcome without duplicate external dispatch. Use existing registered cases when they cover the change; add only cases for actual migration/semantic gaps.\n- Explicitly run the qualified disposable Secret Service cases, including `disposable_secret_service_restart_and_failures` and `disposable_registry_publication_cli_and_retirement_restart`, with an owned bus/keyring/TMPDIR and the actual candidate CONNECTORS_TEST_CLI. Ordinary tests ignore these and cannot substitute for them. Preserve the admitted GNOME Keyring binding and credential redaction controls. Teardown only exact owned children/state after terminal checks.\n- Validate/generate every affected shared/native ESS root and CLI binding under the exact pin; generated drift and both lockfile/workspace builds pass. Demonstrate the retained AEP correction or its verified upstream equivalent.\n- Run the exact full `cargo run --locked -p connectors-build -- gate --msrv`, including applicable runtime1.91 and retained pure minima. No waiver for strict checks, boundaries, pin mismatch, missing roots or excluded workspace. Run affected documentation/website validation if its authored surface changes, as repository instructions require.\n- Produce one final report with requirement-to-entrypoint-to-evidence mapping, exact baseline/final source and dependency pins, source/generated/check manifests, commands/exits, remaining external limitations, and owned-resource teardown. Preserve all unrelated source/planning and baseline integrity. Root then freezes and independently examines the whole delivery under the existing orchestration rules; author completion does not imply provider qualification or integration.\n\nDo not keep extending the